notes               = "Untitled in source. Seven short lines, and the turn is in the last one: the desert gets everything it wanted, and what it wanted was to be thirsty. شصت سال is the round figure again (see also 163, 181, 183). Bare year ۱۳۸۳ → +621 = 2004. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben. Photo check 2026-07-31 (p190): the page prints تشنه باران with no ezāfe hamza — in a book whose typesetter does mark تشنهٔ (p78, old-blue) — light typographic evidence for کویرِ تشنه، باران شد ('the thirsty desert became rain') over کویر، تشنهٔ باران شد ('became thirsty for rain'). Both readings stay live for the translator."
draft               = true

===persian===

شصت سال گذشت
شبی باران
بر کویر بارید.
کویر
هرچه می‌خواست
آن شد.
کویر تشنه باران شد...
تهران ۱۳۸۳

===machine===

Sixty years went by.
One night the rain
fell on the desert.
The desert
became
whatever it had wanted.
The desert became thirsty for rain...
Tehran 1383

===lantern===

Sixty years went by.
One night the rain
fell on the desert.
The desert
became
whatever it had wanted.
The desert became thirsty for rain...

Tehran 1383

===translation===

===footnotes===

The desert is granted its wish and the wish turns out to be the thirst itself, not the
water. Which makes the sixty years in the first line a description of the same arrangement.
